1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[narrator] In order to become kings,

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
the Chimera Ants
have spread across the world,

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
committing acts of utmost tyranny
wherever they go.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
[imperceptible]

5
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
[gasps] Huh?

6
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Huh?

7
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
[Flutter] Huh?

8
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Ah, is that all? I see.

9
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,000
[gasps]

10
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,000
[both gasp]

11
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[opening theme music playing]

12
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
[singer singing in English]

13
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
[singer singing in English]

14
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

15
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
INFILTRATION X AND X SELECTION

16
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
[Gon] Informants?

17
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
[Killua] Yeah.
Expose an enemy spy, get a reward.

18
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
When they rack up enough informant points,
the entire group is promoted.

19
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:54,000
But you commit a crime,
or you provide them false intel,

20
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
then the entire group is given punishment.

21
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Carrot and stick, huh?

22
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,000
so if a whole group tries to escape,
their remaining family can be executed

23
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,000
or imprisoned for life.

24
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
If a family is caught
trying to escape together,

25
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
they'll be executed on the spot.

26
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
making up false stories like,

27
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,000
"In other countries, half the people
starve to death before age ten."

28
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Foreign aid
never gets to those who need it.

29
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
which they're using as a bargaining chip
in international politics,

30
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Uh, no, I think I'm okay.

31
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
That was just a whole lot to take in.

32
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
and he probably heard it from Grandpa.

33
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Oh. Yeah?

34
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Yeah. A long time ago,

35
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
he had to infiltrate the place
in order to finish a job he was doing.

36
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
And I saw similar information

37
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,000
when I was looking around
the Hunter website.

38
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
The same system might still be in place.

39
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
-A town.
-Yeah, a tiny one.

40
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:54,000
They might also have certain practices
in place to root out suspected spies.

41
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Wait here, okay?

42
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[Killua] Nuh-uh.
Something's happened here.

43
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
-Someone's trying to hide it.
-Huh?

44
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
And they did a sloppy job, too.

45
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
[grunts]

46
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
But what's going on here?

47
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
I think this is
the true purpose of the rally.

48
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,000
When whole towns disappear,
nobody will even be suspicious.

49
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
They set it up perfectly.

50
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
The selection has begun.

51
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
All told,
that's about five million people.

52
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Clearing out one town or city at a time
is more effective.

53
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:53,000
In that case, their concern
would just be coworkers or family,

54
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,000
anyone who would notice them missing.

55
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
But with everything going on
with the national rally,

56
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
and not getting in touch
wouldn't be suspicious at all.

57
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
The selection should go smoothly.

58
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:22,000
The capital city of Peijing
is in the southeast corner.

59
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
They'd need to start with western towns
and work east.

60
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
troublesome communication
between the villages

61
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
they can eliminate
any cause for commotion.

62
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
-But…
-[Killua] Hmm?

63
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
[Gon] That means they have to run
all around the country

64
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
to attack
all five million citizens, right?

65
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:58,000
If only 1% survives,
that gives them 50,000 soldiers.

66
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
Yeah, I know, but I mean before that.

67
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
then you'd probably need
a whole lot of help, wouldn't you?

68
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Okay, so let's say that in ten days,

69
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
one Nen user can check 10,000 citizens.

70
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
That's, uh…

71
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[groans]

72
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
-It's 500.
-Yeah, that.

73
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
[Killua] There can't be
that many Ants that can use Nen.

74
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
-Is that what you're saying?
-[Gon] Yeah.

75
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
I agree with you,
but it won't be that hard.

76
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,000
It isn't like they need Nen users
in order to check everyone out.

77
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
[gasps]

78
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
It's what that Chimera Ant used.

79
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
I'm guessing that it can automate victims

80
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:05,000
or, like Genthru's power,
control multiple people at once.

81
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
so the Manipulator
could force a victim's aura

82
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
to concentrate in his fist.

83
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:19,000
One punch alone
could easily create an army of 50,000,

84
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
[grunts]

85
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[Killua] Well, it isn't all bad news.

86
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
If my theory's correct, this'll be easy.

87
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:39,000
We just cause a commotion,
and the selection will totally stop.

88
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
And then after that,

89
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
this'll all be a cinch.

90
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:03,000
You and I will just run around taking them
down one after another and wreaking havoc.

91
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Right!

92
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
The problem is they'll detect us quickly.

93
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,000
[groans]

94
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Once we make our move, they'll know.

95
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
If we want to go through
with the old man's plan,

96
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
then we should try to keep
as low a profile as we possibly can.

97
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
[Gon grunts]

98
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:39,000
If the selection really has already begun,
we can't just simply ignore it.

99
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
I'm with you. Let's go.

100
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
-Okay.
-But I'm gonna do it alone.

101
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,000
-Huh?
-You stay hidden.

102
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Stay hidden?
But wouldn't it be better if we--

103
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Don't forget our primary mission.

104
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
We have to take Pitou down.

105
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
That should be your focus.

106
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
You let me handle
everything else, all right?

107
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
[groans] Yeah, I get it.

108
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
-Do you?
-Huh?

109
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Do you really think you get it?

110
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Killua.

111
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
[clenching]

112
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Then promise me something!

113
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Don't make a move,

114
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
even if people are killed
right in front of you.

115
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Promise me.

116
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
[gasps]

117
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,000
[grunts]

118
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
[gasps]

119
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
[sighs] I'll text you, okay?

120
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Killua?

121
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Sorry. Don't worry about it.
I'm just a little on edge.

122
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[grunts softly]

123
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[chuckles]

124
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[man] What's this?

125
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
They're not citizens of this country.
That's for sure.

126
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:25,000
They look a little young to be spies,
but they're definitely strong.

127
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Are they here to hunt down the King?

128
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
If so, I can't ignore them,

129
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
but I definitely don't want to fight
both of them at once,

130
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:42,000
or the silver-haired one on the left
at all.

131
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
I can tell he's strong
by the way he walks.

132
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
He might even rival a squadron leader.

133
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[man gasps]

134
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
That kid is extraordinary.

135
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,000
[man chuckles]

136
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Well, that's convenient.

137
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
[chorus playing on phonograph]

138
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
we will both find ourselves
in difficult positions.

139
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
[sighs]

140
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Everything, all of it,

141
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
And don't forget
all our lives are on the line here too.

142
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,000
"Diego has committed"?
Like you're so innocent.

143
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:34,000
The wine you're drinking,
even the room you're standing in,

144
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,000
You mean, "We've committed,"
you son of a bitch.

145
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Now then, Mr. Marcos,

146
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
[Knuckle] I don't like it.

147
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Will you please calm yourself down?

148
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
and only 1% of them will survive!

149
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Your point?

150
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:34,000
That means 495,000 people
have already been killed!

151
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
How can you be so damn calm?

152
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Because if we lose our cool now,
it's a death sentence for billions more.

153
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,000
[Knuckle grunts angrily]

154
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
If this plan fails, then everybody dies,

155
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
and if we can't draw
the three Royal Guards away,

156
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
then even Chairman Netero
can't defeat the King.

157
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
So no matter what, we can't afford
to let them discover our existence

158
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,000
-[Knuckle growls]
-You must endure.

159
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
[Shoot] That's right.

160
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
[gasps]

161
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:22,000
If blaming me consoles you at all,
then go ahead.

162
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
But unless you've come up
with a better idea,

163
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
I would advise you
not to be too self-righteous.

164
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,000
[growls]

165
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
[fruit crunches]

166
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[Gon] I hope Killua's okay.

167
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,000
He was acting kinda weird.

168
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Maybe I should have stayed with him.

169
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
But if I'd followed him,
I bet he'd be pretty mad.

170
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,000
[gasps]

171
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[growls]

172
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
-[grunts]
-[gasps]

173
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
You're not crushing me.

174
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
[Gon] It's a good thing
he seems to have the genes of a snake.

175
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,000
I really need to hide better.

176
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
But it's strange.

177
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Why are there still soldier ants

178
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
in an area
they've already finished sorting?

179
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Maybe there are extra lookouts here
because we're pretty near the border.

180
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,000
[grunts]

181
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
[wings flapping]

182
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[upbeat music playing]

183
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:35,000
[Gon] Next time,
"Combination and Evolution."

184
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Step right up!
This is a perfectly ordinary box,

185
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
but say the magic words--

186
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[Killua] Wouldn't that be an illusion?

187
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
